---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { PRIVACY_POLICY_UPDATED, SITE } from "@/consts";
import { displayDate, isoDate } from "@/lib/dates";
---

<LegalLayout
  text="Privacy"
  accent="Policy"
  description="How pa-tech.dev handles your data: no cookies, no analytics, no tracking. What the host processes, the theme setting, and email."
>
  <p>
    Last updated:{" "}
    <time datetime={isoDate(PRIVACY_POLICY_UPDATED)}>
      {displayDate(PRIVACY_POLICY_UPDATED, "long")}
    </time>
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is responsible for this website. This is a personal site; I
    offer no goods or services through it. You can reach me at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies. It has no analytics, tracking, forms or
    third-party content. To deliver the pages, the host processes your IP
    address. It does not store it after the request, and I see no IP addresses
    or visit logs.
  </p>

  <h2>Theme setting</h2>
  <p>
    When you switch between the light and dark theme, your browser stores that
    choice under the key "theme" in localStorage, so the next page opens in the
    same theme. It stays on your device. If you do not want it stored, leave the
    theme switch alone, or clear the site data in your browser to remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Writing to me</h2>
  <p>
    If you email me, I use your address and your message only to reply. I delete
    them when the conversation is over, unless the law requires me to keep them.
  </p>

  <h2>Recipients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      statichost.eu, Sweden, hosts the site under a data processing agreement.
      It uses Hetzner Online GmbH, Germany, and BunnyWay d.o.o., Slovenia.
    </li>
    <li>Proton AG, Switzerland, handles my email.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your data stays in Switzerland and the EEA. I share it with no one else.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
